{
  "glossary": [
    {
      "definition": "(A) \"License\" means an authorization evidenced by a license, certificate, registration, permit, card, or other authority that is issued or conferred by a licensing agency to a licensee or to an applicant for an initial license by which the licensee or initial license applicant has or claims the privilege to engage in a profession, occupation, or occupational activity, or, except in the case of the state dental board, to have control of and operate certain specific equipment, machinery, or premises, over which the licensing agency has jurisdiction.",
      "id": "4776.01-license",
      "normalized": "license",
      "scope": "As used in this chapter:",
      "section": "4776.01",
      "source_title": "Section 4776.01 - Criminal records checks definitions.",
      "source_url": "https://codes.ohio.gov/ohio-revised-code/section-4776.01",
      "term": "License"
    },
    {
      "definition": "(B) Except as provided in section 4776.20 of the Revised Code, \"licensee\" means the person to whom the license is issued by a licensing agency. \"Licensee\" includes a person who, for purposes of section 3796.13 of the Revised Code, has complied with sections 4776.01 to 4776.04 of the Revised Code and has been determined by the division of cannabis control, as the applicable licensing agency, to meet the requirements for employment.",
      "id": "4776.01-licensee",
      "normalized": "licensee",
      "scope": "As used in this chapter:",
      "section": "4776.01",
      "source_title": "Section 4776.01 - Criminal records checks definitions.",
      "source_url": "https://codes.ohio.gov/ohio-revised-code/section-4776.01",
      "term": "licensee"
    },
    {
      "definition": "(C) Except as provided in section 4776.20 of the Revised Code, \"licensing agency\" means any of the following:\n\n(1) The board authorized by Chapters 4701., 4717., 4725., 4729., 4730., 4731., 4732., 4734., 4740., 4741., 4747., 4751., 4753., 4755., 4757., 4759., 4760., 4761., 4762., 4772., 4774., 4778., 4779., and 4783. of the Revised Code to issue a license to engage in a specific profession, occupation, or occupational activity, or to have charge of and operate certain specific equipment, machinery, or premises.\n\n(2) The state dental board, relative to its authority to issue a license pursuant to section 4715.12 , 4715.16 , 4715.21 , or 4715.27 of the Revised Code;\n\n(3) The division of marijuana control, relative to its authority under Chapter 3796. of the Revised Code and any rules adopted under that chapter with respect to a person who is subject to section 3796.13 of the Revised Code;\n\n(4) The director of agriculture, relative to the director's authority to issue licenses under Chapter 928. of the Revised Code.",
      "id": "4776.01-licensing-agency",
      "normalized": "licensing agency",
      "scope": "As used in this chapter:",
      "section": "4776.01",
      "source_title": "Section 4776.01 - Criminal records checks definitions.",
      "source_url": "https://codes.ohio.gov/ohio-revised-code/section-4776.01",
      "term": "licensing agency"
    },
    {
      "definition": "(D) \"Applicant for an initial license\" includes persons seeking a license for the first time and persons seeking a license by reciprocity, endorsement, or similar manner of a license issued in another state. \"Applicant for an initial license\" also includes a person who, for purposes of section 3796.13 of the Revised Code, is required to comply with sections 4776.01 to 4776.04 of the Revised Code.",
      "id": "4776.01-applicant-for-an-initial-license",
      "normalized": "applicant for an initial license",
      "scope": "As used in this chapter:",
      "section": "4776.01",
      "source_title": "Section 4776.01 - Criminal records checks definitions.",
      "source_url": "https://codes.ohio.gov/ohio-revised-code/section-4776.01",
      "term": "Applicant for an initial license"
    },
    {
      "definition": "(E) \"Applicant for a restored license\" includes persons seeking restoration of a license under section 4730.14 , 4730.28 , 4731.222 , 4731.281 , 4759.062 , 4759.063 , 4760.06 , 4760.061 , 4761.06 , 4761.061 , 4762.06 , 4762.061 , 4772.08 , 4772.082 , 4774.06 , 4774.061 , 4778.07 , or 4778.071 of the Revised Code. \"Applicant for a restored license\" does not include a person seeking restoration of a license under section 4751.33 of the Revised Code.",
      "id": "4776.01-applicant-for-a-restored-license",
      "normalized": "applicant for a restored license",
      "scope": "As used in this chapter:",
      "section": "4776.01",
      "source_title": "Section 4776.01 - Criminal records checks definitions.",
      "source_url": "https://codes.ohio.gov/ohio-revised-code/section-4776.01",
      "term": "Applicant for a restored license"
    },
    {
      "definition": "(F) \"Criminal records check\" has the same meaning as in section 109.572 of the Revised Code.\n\nLast updated January 14, 2026 at 10:32 AM",
